{
  "problem": "A traditional recipe makes 24 empanadas (a Spanish snack) using 360 grams of flour. You want to prepare 18 empanadas for a school event. (a) How many grams of flour should you use? (b) If you only have 250 grams of flour, what is the greatest whole number of empanadas you can still bake? Show your reasoning.",
  "answer": "a) 270 grams; b) 16 empanadas",
  "solution_steps": [
    "Find the amount of flour needed for one empanada: 360 g ÷ 24 = 15 g per empanada.",
    "For part (a), multiply the flour per empanada by the desired number: 15 g × 18 = 270 g.",
    "For part (b), divide the flour you have by the flour per empanada: 250 g ÷ 15 g ≈ 16.66.",
    "Since you can only make whole empanadas, take the integer part: 16 empanadas."
  ]
}

