(b) Give the ratio of the outer circumference (the edge of the walkway) to the inner circumference (the edge of the fountain), in simplest exact form.", "answer":"Width ≈ 83 cm; Ratio of outer to inner circumference = √2", "solution_steps":["Let the radius of the fountain be r = 2 m. The outer radius of the walkway is R = r + w.", "Area of the fountain: A_f = πr².", "Area of the whole figure (fountain + walkway): A_total = πR² = π(r + w)².", "Area of the walkway alone: A_walk = A_total – A_f = π[(r + w)² – r²] = π(2rw + w²).", "Given that A_walk = A_f, set π(2rw + w²) = πr² and cancel π: 2rw + w² = r².", "Substitute r = 2 m: w² + 4w – 4 = 0.", "Solve the quadratic: w = [-4 ± √(4² – 4·1·(‑4))]/2 = [-4 ± √32]/2 = -2 ± 2√2.", "Discard the negative root; take w = -2 + 2√2 metres.", "Compute numeric value: w ≈ -2 + 2·1.414 = 0.828 m.", "Convert to centimeters: 0.828 m × 100 = 82.8 cm ≈ 83 cm (nearest cm).", "Outer circumference C_outer = 2πR = 2π(r + w).", "Inner circumference C_inner = 2πr.", "Ratio C_outer / C_inner = (r + w)/r = 1 + w/r.", "Using w = -2 + 2√2 and r = 2: w/r = (-2 + 2√2)/2 = -1 + √2.", "Thus ratio = 1 + (‑1 + √2) = √2.", "Therefore the ratio of the outer to inner circumference simplifies to √2."]}

